## BESTTAXA in RStudio

## Linux Workflow

### Taxonomic classification using three reference databases

The representative sequences (rep-seqs) generated during the DADA2 denoising process were used as input:

- `3-rep-seqs-dada2_FINAL_F.qza` (the filename depends on your files)
- `2-table-dada2_FINAL_F.qza` (the filename depends on your files)

## 1. Taxonomic classification with SILVA

Command used:

```bash
qiime feature-classifier classify-sklearn \
  --i-classifier silva-138-99-nb-classifier.qza \
  --i-reads 3-rep-seqs-dada2_FINAL_F.qza \
  --p-n-jobs 4 \
  --o-classification taxonomy-silva.qza
```

## 2. Taxonomic classification with Greengenes2 (GG2)

Command used:

```bash
qiime feature-classifier classify-sklearn \
  --i-classifier gg2_2024.09_full_length_classifier.qza \
  --i-reads 3-rep-seqs-dada2_FINAL_F.qza \
  --p-n-jobs 4 \
  --o-classification taxonomy-gg2.qza
```

## 3. Taxonomic classification with GTDB

Command used:

```bash
qiime feature-classifier classify-sklearn \
  --i-classifier gtdb_human_stool_weighted_classifier_r220.qza \
  --i-reads 3-rep-seqs-dada2_FINAL_F.qza \
  --p-n-jobs 4 \
  --o-classification taxonomy-gtdb.qza
```

## 4. Exporting the results

The results of each taxonomic classification were exported in TSV format for subsequent integration:

```bash
qiime tools export \
  --input-path taxonomy-*.qza \
  --output-path export_dir
```

## 5. Classification output

Three independent taxonomy files were generated using SILVA, Greengenes2, and GTDB. These files were subsequently used as input for constructing the BESTTAXA consensus classification.

